# Conformance probe pack for rulings 15 and 17 of spec 0.7 on the `bits` wire,
# least significant bit first, one byte per word. Public. One kind.
#
#   byte 0      probe.n, the constant 170 (0xAA), the kind's `when` (low
#               nibble 5) and the count of items (bits 0-1), all on the same
#               bits. Encode writes them in the order fields, `const`, `when`,
#               counts (ruling 15), so byte 0 is 0xA4 plus the count.
#   then        one 2-byte item per count: qty, then val. `optional` on val
#               has no effect inside an item (ruling 17): input that ends
#               inside an item is `malformed-wire`.
#
# On decode the `when` fixes the low nibble at 5, so the count read is 1.
format     conformance-groups-rulings-bits
version    0.7.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
word_bytes 1
field   probe.n  0:0:8  uint
const   0:0:8  170
kind    k
when    0:0:4  5
group   probe.items  0:8  item 16  count 0:0:2
  field  probe.qty  0:0:8  uint
  field  probe.val  0:8:8  uint  optional
end
